  "comment": "The answer correctly identifies that the 200 m² house exceeds either stated limit, that the 40 m² garage fits the separate 60 m² allowance, and that a new house requires building permission, but omits the shared well and wastewater requirement.",
  "answer": "**Verdict: Not feasible as described.** The Kumla-Stensta plan description gives a maximum footprint for the house of **180 m² in the northern part** and **160 m² in the southern part**; a 200 m² house exceeds either limit, regardless of being single-storey. [c:4cb664425072e3a7]\n\n**Key rules and constraints:**\n- The plan description says a separate complementary building, such as a garage, may be up to **60 m² in addition**. So a 40 m² garage appears to fit that allowance, subject to the exact plan provisions for your plot. [c:4cb664425072e3a7]\n- The same description says the house must be at least **4 m from the property boundary**; a garage/carport/store must be at least **1.5 m from a neighbouring property boundary**, unless the neighbour agrees otherwise. [c:4cb664425072e3a7]\n- The plan’s **plankarta** is the legally binding document, while the plan description explains the rules. The corpus has the description but not the map, so your plot’s location and exact binding provisions need confirmation. [c:f7d0be9debce5249]\n- A new house requires building permission. A 40 m² garage is above the 30 m² exemption stated for a complementary building within a detailed-plan area, so it should be included in the building-permit application. [c:5d3d8f2cba8bc679; c:c153b69d1648f70b]\n\n**Process and next steps:**\n1. Ask Vallentuna’s building-permit team to confirm from the **Kumla-Stensta plankarta** which part of the plan your plot falls in and the binding area limit.\n2. If you want to stay within the described limits, consider a house footprint of **no more than 180 m² (north) or 160 m² (south)**, with the garage assessed under the separate complementary-building allowance. [c:4cb664425072e3a7]\n3. Apply for building permission with a site plan showing the house, garage and boundary distances. Building permission within a detailed-plan area depends on the proposal not conflicting with the plan. [c:9a534c8969a1e156]\n\n**Uncertainties:** I don’t have your plot designation or the legally binding plan map in the available records. Those are needed to confirm which area limit applies and the exact garage and siting provisions.",
