  "comment": "Etapp 1 permits terraced houses and gives size and plot ranges, but the answer omits the planned house counts and the requirement for a building permit for each building.",
  "answer": "**Verdict: Feasible with conditions** — terraced houses (radhus) are explicitly permitted in Kristineberg Etapp 1; for Etapp 2 or 3, the final detailed plans and their size limits are not yet settled in the available municipal information.\n\n**Key rules and constraints:**\n- In **Etapp 1**, the adopted detailed plan allows both radhus and combined radhus/parhus/kedjehus in designated residential areas. [c:b28b51b90ce65173]\n- The plan description indicates radhus are intended to be **two storeys**, with a building footprint (*byggnadsarea*) generally around **120–140 m²** and plots varying around **250–600 m²**. These are area-wide descriptions, not a guaranteed allowance for every plot. [c:76387a7ad96570c9]\n- Near the nature-value area, the plan describes a lower scale: **maximum 120 m² building area** and **minimum 500 m² plot size**. [c:76387a7ad96570c9] The plan description also gives a maximum ridge height (*nockhöjd*) of **7.5–9 m**, varying by location. [c:1b608d747f89a0f6]\n- The exact permitted size depends on where the plot sits and the applicable map codes and placement rules. So the figures above are a useful guide, but the **plankarta and binding provisions for the particular plot control**.\n- **Etapp 2** is intended to include both apartment and single-family housing, but the municipality says its detailed plan was still being processed after review in summer 2025. [c:97bb4bf7f1f50013] **Etapp 3** is still being planned; the municipality says a detailed plan must be prepared before development, with consultation planned for spring 2027. [c:8942a08d6014023a]\n\n**Process and next steps:**\n1. Identify the specific plot or block and whether it is in Etapp 1, 2, or 3.\n2. For Etapp 1, check that location’s zoning designation and detailed-plan provisions on Vallentuna’s planning map; those determine the binding building area, height, plot and placement limits.\n3. If you are considering Etapp 2 or 3, ask Vallentuna’s planning department about the latest plan proposal and whether radhus are planned for the specific area.\n\n**Uncertainties:** Without a precise plot or block, I cannot determine which Etapp 1 sub-area rules apply. The stated 120–140 m² is the plan description’s general range, not a single maximum applying throughout Kristineberg.",
