  "comment": "The answer gives the main size and cultural-area limits, but incorrectly suggests notification is generally unnecessary and omits neighbours’ consent near a boundary.",
  "answer": "**Verdict: Feasible with conditions** — a 25 m² guest cottage in a Vallentuna detailed-plan area can generally be built without a building permit, provided it meets the statutory limits and the site is not in a specially protected area.\n\n**Key rules and constraints:**\n- Under PBL 9 kap. 4 §, a permit-exempt cottage in a detailed-plan area must have a building area of no more than 30 m², be smaller than the main building, have a ridge height of no more than 4 m, and be placed within the plot. The total building area of the relevant ancillary buildings on the plot must not exceed 45 m²; older permit-exempt buildings count too. [c:c153b69d1648f70b]\n- The cottage must be ancillary to the house. Vallentuna identifies a guest cottage as a type of ancillary building. [c:a1cbd51fb395f18a]\n- Even without a permit, the project must not conflict with the applicable detailed plan. [c:c1626352bdacc7eb]\n- Vallentuna says a building permit is always required in a culturally and historically particularly valuable area. [c:a1cbd51fb395f18a]\n- A simple cottage does not generally require notification, but notification may be needed for installations such as water or sewerage, or ventilation. Do not start an action that does require notification until you have the required start notice (“startbesked”). [c:e2bb583cd77075bd; c:f8721e335c7]\n\n**Process and next steps:**\n1. Check the plot’s total existing ancillary-building area, including older permit-exempt sheds or cottages, and confirm the proposed 25 m² is *building area* (footprint).\n2. Check the detailed plan and whether the property is in a culturally and historically particularly valuable area. Vallentuna’s building-permit service can help verify this for your property.\n3. If the cottage will have water/sewerage or ventilation, ask the municipality whether notification and a startbesked are required before work begins.\n\n**Uncertainties:** Without your property designation or address, I can’t check the specific detailed-plan provisions or whether the property is in a protected cultural area.",
